My point is, that even if you *don't* combine the commands, Nethack can
choose to *understand* what you mean instead of being obstinate. If you
happen to try to R)emove armor, the armor should be removed. What's
more, Nethack *knows* the commands are related, because if you do it
wrong, it tells you:

Use the 'T' command to take that off.
Use the 'W' command to wear that.
Use the 'P' command to put that on.
Use the 'R' command to remove that.

It's like when you press "r" to read ((or "t" to throw)), it lists only
readable items, but if you press the inventory letter corresponding to
your T-shirt, you can read that too! Similarly, if you press "T" to take
something off, it can list your worn armor, but if you press the letter
corresponding to something that can be R)emoved, it can take that off
too. This works because there are no items that can be both W)orn and
P)ut on to different effect. After all, in other circumstances Nethack
*does* try to make it easier for you, you can for instance both a)pply
and P)ut on a blindfold.

